  "version": "1.0.0",
  "maintainer": "Prof. Shahab Anbarjafari",
  "purpose": "Controlled procurement vocabulary for the Fortum AI procurement agents. Entries here are resolved deterministically and never consume a language-model token, so extending this file is the cheapest available way to raise output quality. Bump `version` on every change: the value is written into every output row so a result can always be traced back to the vocabulary that produced it.",
  "notes": [
    "`phrases` are matched before `terms`, longest first, on the normalised (lower-cased, accent-preserving) text.",
    "`terms` are matched against both the raw token and its stem, so inflected Finnish and Swedish forms resolve without an entry per case.",
    "`compound_parts` drive the Nordic compound splitter: 'asbestipurkutyo' decomposes to asbesti + purku + tyo.",
    "Targets are written in lower case; the description synthesiser applies casing.",
    "`legal_forms` holds incorporation suffixes only. A word that distinguishes one company from another does not belong here: strip 'Nordic' from a vendor name and 'Nordic Cleaning Oy' becomes indistinguishable from 'Cleaning International AB'. Geographic and market qualifiers go in `geographic_qualifiers`, which supplier matching treats as weak rather than absent."
  ],

